Guided Exercise: Container Image Identity and Tags
Objectives
•	Inspect container images by tag and SHA ID.
•	Deploy applications using image tags or SHA IDs.
•	Understand the difference between floating tags (like latest) and immutable references (SHA digests).
•	Observe how OpenShift handles image updates and scaling with different tags.
________________________________________
Step-by-Step Workflow
1.	Setup
o	Start lab: lab start updates-ids
o	Login as developer and select the updates-ids project.
2.	Inspect Images
o	Check the SHA ID for 1-209 and 1-215 tags:
oc image info registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-209 | head
oc image info registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-215 | head
o	Alternative: skopeo inspect docker://registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-215
3.	Deploy Using a Tag
o	Deploy httpd1 using the 1-209 tag:
oc create deployment httpd1 --image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-209
o	Inspect pod to confirm which node and image it is using (crictl ps on node).
4.	Deploy Using SHA ID
o	Retrieve SHA ID in JSON:
IMAGE=$(oc image info registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-209 -o json | jq -r .digest)
o	Deploy httpd2 using the SHA digest:
oc create deployment httpd2 --image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24@$IMAGE
o	Update deployment to a newer image using the 1-215 tag:
oc set image deployment/httpd2 httpd-24=registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-215
5.	Using the latest Tag
o	Assign latest to the old image (1-209) and deploy httpd3:
skopeo copy docker://registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:1-209 docker://registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24:latest
oc create deployment httpd3 --image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/ubi8/httpd-24
o	Reassign latest to a newer image (1-215).
o	Scale httpd3 to two replicas:
oc scale deployment/httpd3 --replicas 2
o	Observe inconsistent pod images:
	Original pod → old image (SHA b1e3...f876)
	New pod → new image (SHA 91ad...fd83)
________________________________________
Key Takeaways
•	SHA IDs are immutable and guarantee the exact image version.
•	Tags like latest are floating; they can point to different images over time, causing inconsistencies in scaled deployments.
•	Using SHA IDs in production ensures all replicas use the same image version.
•	Scaling deployments with floating tags can lead to pods running different image versions.
•	Tools used:
o	oc image info → inspect tag or SHA ID.
o	skopeo inspect → inspect remote registry images.
o	crictl → inspect container images and running pods on nodes.

